---
description: Keep Cargo and RPM build output on disk, never on /tmp
alwaysApply: true
---

# Build output stays on disk

`/tmp` is RAM on Fedora. Do not put compiler output or RPM build trees there.

- Before any `cargo` command, set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` to the workspace `target/` directory. That overrides a sandbox cache under `/tmp/cursor-sandbox-cache`. `.cargo/config.toml` already names `target/`; the environment variable wins over that file, so set the variable explicitly.
- Run `rpmbuild` with `_topdir` at `dist/rpmbuild` or `~/rpmbuild`. Do not use `/tmp/linux-vault-rpmbuild-*`.
- The spec unsets `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` inside `%build` so the package build stays inside that `_topdir`. Leave that unset in place.
